# Who approves what. GitHub requires a review from every owner matched by a
# changed path; the LAST matching pattern wins, so order here is meaningful:
# broad defaults first, narrow territory last.
#
# !! USER-OWNED REPO — USERNAMES, NOT TEAM SLUGS !!
# `osxsystem/skills` is owned by a user account, and `@org/team` slugs only
# exist under a GitHub organization — on this repo a team slug matches nothing
# and the rule FAILS OPEN (GitHub requests no review at all). Until the repo
# moves to an org, every owner below is a username with write access.
#
# Upgrade path, when the repo transfers to an `osxsystem` org:
#   1. Create teams: maintainers, mobile, platform (one per block below).
#   2. Swap each username for its team slug — and, in the same change, the
#      `owner:` field of every entry in `.fork/catalog.yaml`, which mirrors
#      this file. Regenerate CATALOG.md.
# The per-path blocks are already shaped for that swap; only the right-hand
# column changes.

# Default: anything not claimed below is a maintainers call.
*                                   @osxsystem

# --- Upstream territory (byte-frozen vendor files) --------------------------
# Edits here are boundary changes, not content changes: every one of them has
# to be sanctioned in `.fork/sanctioned-edits.txt` and survive a sync. Reviewed
# by maintainers, who carry the sync context — see `.fork/sync-playbook.md`.
/skills/engineering/                @osxsystem
/skills/productivity/               @osxsystem
/skills/misc/                       @osxsystem
/skills/in-progress/                @osxsystem
/skills/deprecated/                 @osxsystem
/docs/engineering/                  @osxsystem
/docs/productivity/                 @osxsystem

# --- Fork control plane, harness, and CI ------------------------------------
/.fork/                             @osxsystem
/scripts/                           @osxsystem
/.github/                           @osxsystem

# --- Team domains -----------------------------------------------------------
# One block per existing domain under `skills/team/`: the skills and the docs
# tree that mirrors them. A new domain folder adds a block here, a matching
# `owner:` in `.fork/catalog.yaml`, and nothing else. Add each discipline's
# usernames here as they gain write access (space-separated on the same line).
/skills/team/mobile/                @osxsystem
/docs/team/mobile/                  @osxsystem

/skills/team/platform/              @osxsystem
/docs/team/platform/                @osxsystem
